Ping away!

535
00:36:15,612 --> 00:36:17,881
Ok, we got something.

536
00:36:17,915 --> 00:36:19,283
What is that?

537
00:36:19,316 --> 00:36:20,350
Moving off
the port side.

538
00:36:20,384 --> 00:36:22,853
Salvanto, identify.

539
00:36:22,886 --> 00:36:24,588
Identifying.

540
00:36:26,957 --> 00:36:28,992
It--It's nothing, sir.

541
00:36:29,026 --> 00:36:30,561
Nothing? But--

542
00:36:30,594 --> 00:36:32,563
What do you--
What does that mean?

543
00:36:32,596 --> 00:36:33,664
There's
no signature match.

544
00:36:33,697 --> 00:36:37,601
We've never had
a sonar reading
like this before.

545
00:36:37,634 --> 00:36:38,869
Whatever it is, though,

546
00:36:38,902 --> 00:36:43,407
It's sitting
off the port side
about 200 hundred meters.

547
00:36:43,440 --> 00:36:44,775
And it's not moving.

548
00:36:44,808 --> 00:36:47,578
Mr. Brickman, is there
any chance we can
turn around to face it?

549
00:36:47,611 --> 00:36:49,479
Negative.

550
00:36:49,513 --> 00:36:52,382
Not on these rudders.

551
00:36:53,083 --> 00:36:55,018
What are we
gonna do, sir?

552
00:36:55,052 --> 00:37:00,324
Sir, we can't just
leave them out there.

553
00:37:11,335 --> 00:37:12,569
Sir?

554
00:37:12,970 --> 00:37:15,472
Mr. Brickman...

555
00:37:17,407 --> 00:37:23,013
take us down.
Go silent.

556
00:37:27,484 --> 00:37:29,519
You heard the man.

557
00:37:29,553 --> 00:37:34,424
Full power. Let's hope
these rudders hold up.

558
00:37:53,877 --> 00:37:56,079
Excuse me, captain,
i hate to point this out,

559
00:37:56,113 --> 00:37:58,048
But now might be
a really good time
to call for help.

560
00:37:58,081 --> 00:38:00,817
I'm well aware
of our situation,
special agent turner.

561
00:38:00,851 --> 00:38:02,719
And while i appreciate
your enthusiasm
and concern,

562
00:38:02,753 --> 00:38:05,455
I really think it's best
if you took care
of your business

563
00:38:05,489 --> 00:38:06,723
And you let me
take care of mine.

564
00:38:06,757 --> 00:38:08,392
Look, shaw,
i know your game.

565
00:38:08,425 --> 00:38:10,394
I know
all about you.

566
00:38:10,427 --> 00:38:11,094
Oh, really?

567
00:38:11,128 --> 00:38:12,529
We are obviously
in trouble.

568
00:38:12,562 --> 00:38:15,799
Now is not the time
to try to be a hero.

569
00:38:15,832 --> 00:38:17,000
Hero?

570
00:38:17,034 --> 00:38:20,971
And what the hell
do you think
you'd know about that?

571
00:38:22,773 --> 00:38:24,941
Agent turner, report to the brig.

572
00:38:24,975 --> 00:38:28,378
Agent turner,
report to the brig.

573
00:38:28,412 --> 00:38:30,981
Yeah,
i'll be right there.

574
00:38:47,130 --> 00:38:48,465
Hey, um, brickman,

575
00:38:48,498 --> 00:38:52,969
Is there any way i can
get a copy of those tapes
from the divers?

576
00:38:53,003 --> 00:38:54,538
Why don't you talk
to the captain?

577
00:38:54,571 --> 00:38:57,007
No, listen, listen,
i think i can help here.

578
00:38:57,040 --> 00:38:59,109
Hey, lady, in case
you haven't noticed,

579
00:38:59,142 --> 00:39:02,813
We just lost a couple
of good men out there.

580
00:39:02,846 --> 00:39:03,914
And in case
you haven't noticed,

581
00:39:03,947 --> 00:39:05,348
You need all the help
you can get,

582
00:39:05,382 --> 00:39:08,552
So i suggest that you
tell me how i can get
a copy of those tapes.

583
00:39:08,585 --> 00:39:10,187
Hey, hey.
You want 'em?
It's all digital.

584
00:39:10,220 --> 00:39:11,755
Log on to the ship's
mainframe and--

585
00:39:11,788 --> 00:39:13,657
What are you doing, man?
We're in trouble here.

586
00:39:13,690 --> 00:39:15,992
We don't have time
to mess around with--

587
00:39:16,026 --> 00:39:17,561
Taylor!

588
00:39:19,162 --> 00:39:21,498
Enough.

589
00:39:22,132 --> 00:39:23,767
Great.

590
00:39:25,135 --> 00:39:26,636
Brickman, i just--

591
00:39:26,670 --> 00:39:28,105
Not now.

592
00:39:31,541 --> 00:39:33,043
Hold on. Hold on!

593
00:39:33,076 --> 00:39:35,779
It's gonna be ok.

594
00:39:39,182 --> 00:39:40,083
What the hell's
going on?

595
00:39:40,117 --> 00:39:42,486
I don't know, sir.
I found him this way.

596
00:39:42,519 --> 00:39:44,121
He's--He's
going into shock.

597
00:39:44,154 --> 00:39:45,055
He's choking.

598
00:39:45,088 --> 00:39:47,824
Just be careful.
Be very careful with him.

599
00:39:47,858 --> 00:39:49,559
Ohh! Uhh!

600
00:39:49,593 --> 00:39:50,627
Aah! Aah!

601
00:39:50,660 --> 00:39:56,500
Uh-Oh. Looks like
we're in trouble
again, roy.

602
00:39:57,234 --> 00:40:00,971
Wait a minute.
What the hell was that?

603
00:40:01,004 --> 00:40:03,507
Ok, wait, back up.

604
00:40:07,010 --> 00:40:10,480
Oh, god.

605
00:40:10,514 --> 00:40:11,481
Uh, roger that.

606
00:40:11,515 --> 00:40:13,950
Mr. Brickman,
engines full up,
300 meters.

607
00:40:13,984 --> 00:40:15,152
Aye-Aye, sir.

608
00:40:15,185 --> 00:40:16,853
There's a mountain range
about 7 kilometers
ahead of us.

609
00:40:16,887 --> 00:40:19,256
Now, if i can get us moving
in a straight line,

610
00:40:19,289 --> 00:40:22,225
We can run for the hills
and see if this thing follows.

611
00:40:22,259 --> 00:40:26,096
Dropping remote
detonation mines
as we go?

612
00:40:26,129 --> 00:40:28,165
What do you think?

613
00:40:28,598 --> 00:40:31,268
In these canyons,
i'd say you're crazy,

614
00:40:31,301 --> 00:40:33,203
But what else is new?

615
00:40:33,236 --> 00:40:36,106
Good.
Let's rock.

616
00:40:36,139 --> 00:40:38,241
You're the captain.

617
00:40:38,275 --> 00:40:39,543
By the way,

618
00:40:39,576 --> 00:40:44,181
Do we know exactly
what it is that's
gonna be following us?

619
00:40:44,214 --> 00:40:46,082
I have no idea,

620
00:40:46,116 --> 00:40:49,953
But it's got a tiger
by the tail.

621
00:40:53,690 --> 00:40:57,194
Salvanto, we're going
into unknown territory.

622
00:40:57,227 --> 00:40:59,563
Let's hope this thing
takes the bait.

623
00:40:59,596 --> 00:41:03,867
And, um, write a letter
to your mama.

624
00:41:12,876 --> 00:41:15,245
If you want him to live,

625
00:41:15,278 --> 00:41:17,013
Just take the keys
and unlock me.

626
00:41:17,047 --> 00:41:21,284
Don't do it, sir.
I'm ready to die.

627
00:41:21,318 --> 00:41:22,953
Ok,
nobody needs to die.

628
00:41:22,986 --> 00:41:25,121
Check this out, sir.

629
00:41:25,155 --> 00:41:27,691
You can still see it.
There!

630
00:41:27,724 --> 00:41:29,326
Mr. Brickman.

631
00:41:29,359 --> 00:41:32,295
Depth--
300 meters, captain.

632
00:41:32,329 --> 00:41:33,730
20 knots and climbing.

633
00:41:33,763 --> 00:41:34,531
20 knots confirmed.

634
00:41:34,564 --> 00:41:37,067
How about a little
loop-De-Loop?

635
00:41:37,100 --> 00:41:37,968
Confuse the mother.

636
00:41:38,001 --> 00:41:39,236
It's moving into position.

637
00:41:39,269 --> 00:41:42,105
Come on. Come on.

638
00:41:42,906 --> 00:41:44,641
We got it.
There. Right there.

639
00:41:44,674 --> 00:41:46,309
Mr. Brickman,
ready the mines.

640
00:41:46,343 --> 00:41:47,244
Aye, sir.

641
00:41:47,277 --> 00:41:48,411
Captain, you are not
gonna believe this.

642
00:41:48,445 --> 00:41:52,282
Listen,
i enhanced the videotape
from lopez and lucas.

643
00:41:52,315 --> 00:41:53,450
As far as i can tell,

644
00:41:53,483 --> 00:41:55,352
We're dealing
with some kind
of giant sea creature.

645
00:41:55,385 --> 00:41:58,288
Oh, good, that makes
my plan a lot easier.

646
00:41:58,321 --> 00:41:59,356
What plan?

647
00:41:59,389 --> 00:42:03,193
The one where i'm gonna
blow it out of the water.

648
00:42:03,226 --> 00:42:06,263
This thing's getting
better by the minute.

649
00:42:09,299 --> 00:42:11,167
That-A-Boy.

650
00:42:11,201 --> 00:42:14,671
You see, there is
hope for you yet.

651
00:42:16,273 --> 00:42:19,042
Sir, 200 meters and closing.

652
00:42:19,075 --> 00:42:20,176
Primed and ready.

653
00:42:20,210 --> 00:42:23,280
And...deploy.

654
00:42:23,313 --> 00:42:25,715
175 meters.

655
00:42:25,749 --> 00:42:27,984
Mines away.

656
00:42:30,287 --> 00:42:30,921
And...

657
00:42:30,954 --> 00:42:33,156
125 and closing.

658
00:42:33,189 --> 00:42:34,724
Detonate.

659
00:42:43,199 --> 00:42:44,100
Come on.

660
00:42:44,134 --> 00:42:46,069
Did we get it?

661
00:42:48,004 --> 00:42:49,406
Yes! We've got it, sir!

662
00:42:49,439 --> 00:42:51,174
It's disappeared
off the sonar.

663
00:42:51,207 --> 00:42:54,210
Yes! Oh, baby!

664
00:42:54,244 --> 00:42:58,214
You are a man!
You are a very bad man!

665
00:42:58,248 --> 00:43:01,318
I'm a bad man!
I shook up the world!

666
00:43:01,351 --> 00:43:02,752
Whoo!
Whoo!

667
00:43:02,786 --> 00:43:03,687
Ohh! Hmm!

668
00:43:03,720 --> 00:43:05,221
Mr. Brickman,
maintain course and speed.

669
00:43:05,255 --> 00:43:07,290
See how far those rudders
will take us.

670
00:43:07,324 --> 00:43:11,127
What did i tell you?
Tiger by the tail.

671
00:43:11,161 --> 00:43:12,128
Mmm!
Mmm!

672
00:43:12,162 --> 00:43:16,700
Come on, roy,
you know it makes sense.

673
00:43:17,367 --> 00:43:19,302
Good boy.

674
00:43:19,336 --> 00:43:22,072
You've done well.

675
00:43:22,105 --> 00:43:24,441
All right, let him--
Let him go.

676
00:43:24,474 --> 00:43:27,944
They'll get you for this.
You will burn.

677
00:43:27,978 --> 00:43:33,683
Like i said...
not in this lifetime.

678
00:43:33,717 --> 00:43:35,185
Uhh!

679
00:43:36,386 --> 00:43:37,420
Wait, whoa, whoa.

680
00:43:37,454 --> 00:43:40,256
Captain, you're not gonna believe this.

681
00:43:40,290 --> 00:43:43,293
Sir, it's still there.

682
00:43:43,927 --> 00:43:45,795
Oh, my god.
What does it want?

683
00:43:45,829 --> 00:43:48,064
Increase speed,
mr. Brickman.

684
00:43:48,098 --> 00:43:50,300
Yes, sir!

685
00:43:58,174 --> 00:44:00,877
Sir, it's gaining on us.

686
00:44:00,910 --> 00:44:02,712
Speed--46 knots.

687
00:44:02,746 --> 00:44:04,114
Impact in 60 seconds.

688
00:44:04,147 --> 00:44:08,084
Deploy all the mines.
Now.

689
00:44:24,300 --> 00:44:25,869
What the hell
is that?

690
00:44:25,902 --> 00:44:26,836
I don't understand.

691
00:44:26,870 --> 00:44:27,871
Oh, my god.

692
00:44:27,904 --> 00:44:30,040
It's heading straight
for us.

693
00:44:30,073 --> 00:44:30,874
Sir!

694
00:44:30,907 --> 00:44:33,243
Impact in 20 seconds!

695
00:44:33,276 --> 00:44:36,980
19, 18, 17...

696
00:44:37,013 --> 00:44:38,348
Mr. Brickman,
brace yourself.

697
00:44:38,381 --> 00:44:41,217
Everybody maintain
your position.

698
00:44:41,251 --> 00:44:43,186
This is your captain
speaking.

699
00:44:43,219 --> 00:44:44,254
This is an emergency.

700
00:44:44,287 --> 00:44:47,457
Lock down all main valves
and prepare for impact.

701
00:44:47,490 --> 00:44:48,858
Let's seal it.

702
00:44:48,892 --> 00:44:51,027
11... jesus.

703
00:44:51,061 --> 00:44:55,265
10, 9, 8,

704
00:44:55,298 --> 00:44:58,768
7, 6...

705
00:45:00,537 --> 00:45:02,772
Hang on.
3, 2...

706
00:45:02,806 --> 00:45:04,307
everybody hang on!

707
00:45:04,340 --> 00:45:06,176
1, sir!

708
00:45:12,348 --> 00:45:13,550
Hold on!

709
00:45:13,583 --> 00:45:15,318
Sir, we've lost control!

710
00:45:15,351 --> 00:45:17,220
Maintain your stations!

711
00:45:24,194 --> 00:45:25,328
Salvanto,
give me a reading!

712
00:45:25,361 --> 00:45:29,365
Sir, it's got a grip on us!
It won't let go!

713
00:45:29,399 --> 00:45:31,101
Reverse engines full!

714
00:45:31,134 --> 00:45:32,302
We're being pulled down!

715
00:45:32,335 --> 00:45:34,370
We've got
minimal control!

716
00:45:36,005 --> 00:45:38,141
Come on,
move it! Move it!

717
00:45:38,174 --> 00:45:42,011
I can't hold it, sir!
I can't hold it!

718
00:45:42,045 --> 00:45:44,314
Come on!
Come on! Come on!

719
00:45:46,182 --> 00:45:48,218
Do something!

720
00:45:48,251 --> 00:45:49,452
Where? Where is it now?

721
00:45:49,486 --> 00:45:52,322
What is our depth?
What is our depth?

722
00:45:52,355 --> 00:45:54,290
Get me off
this sinking sub!

723
00:45:54,324 --> 00:45:55,525
Get off me!

724
00:45:55,558 --> 00:45:56,459
Taylor, get a grip!

725
00:45:56,493 --> 00:45:57,460
How far are we
from that mountain range?

726
00:45:57,494 --> 00:46:00,096
Oh, sir, we're right on top of it!

727
00:46:00,130 --> 00:46:02,132
We can't avoid it!

728
00:46:03,199 --> 00:46:07,237
Full engines, mr. Brickman!
Nose up! On my order!

729
00:46:07,270 --> 00:46:07,804
Captain!

730
00:46:07,837 --> 00:46:10,273
Engine full! Nose up!

731
00:46:10,306 --> 00:46:11,374
I can't control it!

732
00:46:11,407 --> 00:46:13,276
Speeding up in depth!
We're gonna hit!

733
00:46:13,309 --> 00:46:15,178
750 meters!

734
00:46:15,211 --> 00:46:19,382
Any deeper, and we're
gonna crack like an egg!

735
00:47:22,412 --> 00:47:24,380
Everybody, ok?

736
00:47:25,515 --> 00:47:27,417
Whoo!

737
00:47:27,450 --> 00:47:28,985
You ok?

738
00:47:29,018 --> 00:47:29,886
Yeah.

739
00:47:29,919 --> 00:47:32,455
Mr. Brickman, take a look at this.

740
00:47:32,488 --> 00:47:34,424
Captain...

741
00:47:35,658 --> 00:47:38,027
800 meters.

742
00:47:39,095 --> 00:47:39,829
Mayday, mayday.

743
00:47:39,863 --> 00:47:41,264
This is
the
ssn roosevelt.

744
00:47:41,297 --> 00:47:45,368
We are down.
I repeat, we are down.

745
00:47:45,668 --> 00:47:48,504
I need a drink.

746
00:47:48,538 --> 00:47:53,243
Captain,
we're at crush depth.

747
00:47:53,276 --> 00:47:55,979
She's not gonna hold.

748
00:47:56,679 --> 00:47:57,614
Salvanto.
Sir?

749
00:47:57,647 --> 00:48:01,251
Go check out the damage
in the engine room.

750
00:48:01,284 --> 00:48:03,052
Aye, sir.

751
00:48:04,587 --> 00:48:07,257
You know how to pray,
mr. Brickman?

752
00:48:07,290 --> 00:48:09,192
Now's the time.

753
00:48:09,492 --> 00:48:11,227
¡arriba!

754
00:48:44,727 --> 00:48:45,695
Hello?

755
00:48:51,301 --> 00:48:52,135
Hello?

756
00:48:52,168 --> 00:48:56,306
You fool,
you left the door open.

757
00:48:58,341 --> 00:49:00,443
Room service.

758
00:49:03,780 --> 00:49:04,647
What a mess.

759
00:49:04,681 --> 00:49:08,151
I hope these people
are good tippers.

760
00:49:12,455 --> 00:49:14,457
What is this?

761
00:49:14,657 --> 00:49:17,360
It's your tip.

762
00:49:18,061 --> 00:49:20,430
Aah!

763
00:49:28,404 --> 00:49:29,405
So, get this.

764
00:49:29,439 --> 00:49:30,840
Based on its size
and speed--

765
00:49:30,873 --> 00:49:34,410
I mean, there is
no scientific explanation
for the thing that hit us.

766
00:49:34,444 --> 00:49:35,678
But we know different,
don't we?

767
00:49:35,712 --> 00:49:37,413
We know it's out there,
and we know it's not
too friendly.

768
00:49:37,447 --> 00:49:39,382
You're making an assumption,
captain. It lives here.

769
00:49:39,415 --> 00:49:42,051
You drove a nuclear sub
through its living room.

770
00:49:42,085 --> 00:49:43,019
Yes, if i get
the opportunity,

771
00:49:43,052 --> 00:49:44,287
I'm gonna blow it into
so many little bits,

772
00:49:44,320 --> 00:49:46,089
You'll be able
to open up your own
little sushi restaurant.

773
00:49:46,122 --> 00:49:46,956
You like sushi,
don't you?

774
00:49:46,990 --> 00:49:49,525
What if somebody
walked into your home

775
00:49:49,559 --> 00:49:52,362
And pissed on your carpet?

776
00:49:55,131 --> 00:49:57,433
Forgive me for appearing
to be upset,

777
00:49:57,467 --> 00:49:59,102
But in case
you haven't noticed,

778
00:49:59,135 --> 00:50:00,203
We're stuck
at a depth that...

779
00:50:00,236 --> 00:50:03,639
well, few men get
the opportunity
to experience

780
00:50:03,673 --> 00:50:07,310
Unless...well,
they're about to die.

781
00:50:07,343 --> 00:50:10,680
I just lost 2 men today,
2 very good men.

782
00:50:10,713 --> 00:50:12,415
What?!

783
00:50:13,216 --> 00:50:14,550
Did...did the noise
wake you?

784
00:50:14,584 --> 00:50:18,287
Look, we were attacked
by an underwater creature
of some kind.

785
00:50:18,321 --> 00:50:20,356
I'm still trying to
figure out exactly what.

786
00:50:20,390 --> 00:50:21,724
I don't have time
for this.

787
00:50:21,758 --> 00:50:23,326
When you're finished
with your briefing,
special agent turner,

788
00:50:23,359 --> 00:50:24,761
I'll be down
in the engine room.

789
00:50:24,794 --> 00:50:25,762
I don't need this
right now.

790
00:50:25,795 --> 00:50:28,431
I think it's about time
we stopped playing games

791
00:50:28,464 --> 00:50:29,665
With the rookie
agent, ok?

792
00:50:29,699 --> 00:50:33,403
Casper's gone, and
you got a dead sailor
on your hands.

793
00:50:33,436 --> 00:50:34,070
What do you mean?

794
00:50:34,103 --> 00:50:35,405
He's escaped.
He's gone.

795
00:50:35,438 --> 00:50:38,441
